      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Type 2 diabetes is diagnosed using specific blood tests that measure your blood glucose or average blood sugar levels over time.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "using specific blood tests that measure your blood glucose or average blood sugar levels over time"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Key Diagnostic Blood Tests"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Hemoglobin A1c (HbA1c) Test: Measures your average blood sugar level over the past 2 to 3 months. Does not require fasting.",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Diabetes result: 6.5% or higher"
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Prediabetes result: 5.7% to 6.4%",
                "reference_indexes": [
                  1,
                  2,
                  3,
                  4,
                  5
                ]
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              2,
              3,
              4,
              5
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Fasting Plasma Glucose (FPG) Test: Measures your blood sugar after you do not eat or drink anything (except water) for at least 8 hours.",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Diabetes result: 126 mg/dL (7.0 mmol/L) or higher"
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Prediabetes result: 100 to 125 mg/dL (5.6 to 6.9 mmol/L)",
                "reference_indexes": [
                  1,
                  2,
                  4,
                  6,
                  7
                ]
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              2,
              4,
              6,
              7
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Two-Hour Oral Glucose Tolerance Test (OGTT): Measures your blood sugar before and 2 hours after you drink a special high-sugar liquid (following an 8-hour fast).",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Diabetes result: 200 mg/dL (11.1 mmol/L) or higher",
                "reference_indexes": [
                  1,
                  4
                ]
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              4
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Random Plasma Glucose Test: Measures your blood sugar at any time of day, regardless of when you last ate. Used if you have classic diabetes symptoms (such as extreme thirst or frequent urination).",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Diabetes result: 200 mg/dL (11.1 mmol/L) or higher",
                "reference_indexes": [
                  0,
                  5,
                  8
                ]
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              5,
              8
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Confirmation and Next Steps"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Repeat Testing: Unless you have clear symptoms of high blood sugar combined with a high random reading, doctors usually repeat the test on a second day or use a second test to confirm the diagnosis.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              2,
              4
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Over-the-Counter Meters: Home fingerstick blood glucose meters cannot be used to officially diagnose diabetes; formal lab work is required.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              3,
              9
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "For official guidance and screening recommendations, you can consult the American Diabetes Association Diagnosis Guide or review information via MedlinePlus Diabetes Type 2 .",
